WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:02.935
 Jason, Sam, congratulations.

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:04.070
You guys are moving
on to the third round

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.871
of this competition,
based solely

00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:07.474
on the strength of your blades.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.709
And that's going to play out
very nicely, because, now we're

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.177
sending you back
to your home forges

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:17.250
to recreate one of
these, the spiked mace.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:21.921
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.089
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:32.665
 My general game
plan today is to forge

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.934
and heat treat the spikes.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:38.237
So I got a half inch
round of 4142 steel.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.873
That needs to be
forged down smaller

00:00:40.939 --> 00:00:44.277
and then put the point on it.

00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:45.478
I'm forging them really quick.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.280
I can do them each
in about one heat.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:50.150
I'm heating up my two
rods at the same time.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:53.519
So while I'm working one, the
other one can be heated up.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:56.289
What'll happen next is I'll
forge a little tail end

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.758
and that's what's going
to go into the ball.

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:02.028
This was provided by the judges.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:06.032
I drill the holes on the
center line of the ball.

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:07.633
And I'm just getting so excited.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.834
So I put some spikes in.

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.870
And this thing looks bad ass.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.172
That's pretty damn cool.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.010 line:7%
 It's day one.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:19.345
We're at my home forge
for OTH Forge and Foundry.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.715
Today, I'm going to be
forging out 25 spikes.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:26.052
If I can get all 25 finished,
then I'm going to be well

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:28.354
set up and ahead of the game.

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:29.155
We got one done.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.824
First spike's ready.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:35.060
I'm using the S7 steel,
because it has an incredibly

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.664
high impact
resistance, which lends

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.498
itself to a bludgeoning weapon.

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:40.133
There we go.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.134
Mace spike's done.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.903
So now, I'm going
to mechanically

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.437
attach it to the ball.

00:01:45.537 --> 00:01:48.307 line:0%
Now I'm setting up
my mill to attempt

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:51.377 line:7%
to drill and tap the spikes.

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:54.614 line:0%
I'm going to tap each one of
the spikes out individually,

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.917 line:0%
thread them on stock,
and use that to attach

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.285 line:7%
it to the ball head.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.087
The most concerning
point for me is just

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:03.523
how strong that connection is.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:04.923
If something goes
wrong, it's going

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:08.427
to be a spike breaking off.

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:09.795
Nope.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:13.299
The spike is too hard for
this drill bit to cut into.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:16.335
I need to get each one of
the 25 individual spikes

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.070
attached to the head.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.272
One more time.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:20.639
I'm gonna tap each
one of the spikes

00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:26.045
out individually to attach
it to the ball head.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.313
No.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.216
Two bits down, not
taking down a third one.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.417
Weld them on.

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:34.319
Move on to plan B.
Attach the threads

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.956
with just a basic bead weld.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.224
Weld holds-- you
actually have no idea

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:40.360
how happy that makes me.

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:49.168
 So I'm starting off today
mounting the rest of the spikes

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:50.603
to the other half of the ball.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.672
The fit of these spikes,
what I'm going to be doing

00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:56.642
is putting them through half
of my ball, heating up the end,

00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:00.046
and actually riveting it over
on the inside of the ball.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:03.449
So these spikes are
gonna go nowhere.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.751
Making progress.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:05.951
Only 20 hours left.

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:07.920
Doesn't feel like a ton of time.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.455
Done with all the spikes.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.457
But I think I'll be
able to get done.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.960
You could definitely do
some damage with this.

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:19.799
 Today, I need to attach
the spikes head the mace.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:20.966
After that, it's
gonna be working

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.602
on the guard, the pommel.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.004
Everything fits.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:29.375
And I want to
break a few things.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.477
That passed the test
really, really easy.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:35.114 line:0%
It was a long, very
hard day, but I'm

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:38.984 line:7%
very happy with the results.

00:03:39.084 --> 00:03:40.419 line:7%
 I got a lot done yesterday.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.089
Pretty much just
got to do my handle.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:46.392
What this project needs
is a [inaudible] figure

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.527
8 guard and a knuckle bow.

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.296
That looks freaking awesome.

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:53.599
I'm really, really pleased
with how that guard turned out.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.234
Typically, I try
to make whatever

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.703
I'm making aesthetically
pleasing as possible.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.740
So I decided to put some
decorative little grooves

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.141
in my knuckle bow.

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:04.077
Time to rivet it all together.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.311
I got my knuckle bow
made out of mild steel.

00:04:06.411 --> 00:04:09.348
And I'm attaching it
with copper rivets, disk

00:04:09.414 --> 00:04:11.484
pommel with a wrought iron cap.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.753
It's as secure as I
could've hoped for all.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.188
I have left to do is
put on a leather wrap

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:17.890
and this project is a wrap.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.863 line:0%
 The first thing
I'm gonna do today

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.666 line:0%
is drill a hole through the
head, through the shaft,

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.401 line:0%
and out the other
side of the head,

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:32.105 line:0%
in order to pin this head
into place against the shaft.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.539
I've already welded
the head to the shaft,

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:37.410
but I want to make sure this
ball isn't going anywhere.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.578
That's a spiky murderball.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:43.649
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the Kill Test.

00:04:43.715 --> 00:04:46.618
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:04:46.718 --> 00:04:48.354
I will take your
spike mace and deliver

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:52.224
some killing blows on this
unsuspecting ballistics dummy.

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:53.092
Jason, you're up first.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:53.825
You ready for this?

00:04:53.892 --> 00:04:54.594
 Absolutely.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.361
 Let's do this.

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:23.556
 [bleep].

00:05:28.026 --> 00:05:31.831
 All right, Jason, let's talk
about your spiked mace here.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.400
Your handle construction
fits in my hand nicely.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:37.169
It is a cylindrical handle,
but it's nice enough

00:05:37.235 --> 00:05:38.237
to where I can hold on to it.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.705
There's a good grip to that.

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:43.910
Now, this thing, like you
said, is a murder weapon.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.345
It crushes with every strike.

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:49.548
But in so doing, some
of the spikes came off.

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:52.017
There's about five
pieces missing on this.

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:55.621
But overall, sir, without a
doubt, and a big headache,

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:56.422
it'll kill.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.025
All right, Sam.
It's your turn.

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:01.159
You ready?
- Yes.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:01.894
 Let's do this.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:25.651
All right, Sam.

00:06:25.717 --> 00:06:28.387
Let's talk about
your spike mace here.

00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:30.389
First up, it's a crusher.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.624
It's a heavy forward
weapon, that when

00:06:32.724 --> 00:06:36.194
you're thrusting with it,
it does penetrate easily.

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:38.764
Now, there's an issue here.

00:06:38.864 --> 00:06:42.601
Your handle, it gets in the
way, especially with a very

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.703
forward heavy weapon.

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:46.906
You could potentially hurt
the person wielding it,

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:49.141
which unfortunately
prevents it from being

00:06:49.241 --> 00:06:50.976
a fully functional weapon.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:54.480
But despite that, this
is a sharp weapon.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:58.618
This definitely is something
that will crush and it'll kill.

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:08.093
Bladesmiths, welcome
to our strength test.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.861
I'm gonna take your weapons.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.697
And I'm gonna play a
little terracotta baseball.

00:07:11.763 --> 00:07:14.133
Two things to
remember, it's not what

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:15.935
your weapon does to the jars.

00:07:16.001 --> 00:07:18.137
I want to see what the jars
are gonna do to your weapons.

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:23.041
And number two, I'm gonna
be swinging for the fences.

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:23.843
Jason, you're up.

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:24.510
You ready?

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:25.244
 Let's do it.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:25.978
 Let's go.

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:51.203
You see, on your
head, you've got

00:07:51.303 --> 00:07:55.774
some of these nubs that have
clay in them, some that don't.

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:58.577
The ones that don't,
broke on the pots.

00:07:58.643 --> 00:08:00.379
So you lost a few more spikes.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:03.182
That being said though,
it's comfortable.

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:06.118
I can keep swinging this
weapon for quite a while.

00:08:06.218 --> 00:08:10.122
Even if more spikes came off,
this is still a deadly weapon,

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:12.157
because you got the ball
on here with the nubs

00:08:12.224 --> 00:08:13.392
and your main spike.

00:08:13.458 --> 00:08:15.994
Overall, good job.

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:17.195
Hey, Sam.

00:08:17.262 --> 00:08:18.330
- Hey.
- You ready?

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:19.131
 Oh, yeah.

00:08:19.198 --> 00:08:19.866
 OK.

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:24.436
 I think my spikes
are gonna hold up,

00:08:24.536 --> 00:08:26.471
but I'm really concerned
about my handle.

00:08:26.538 --> 00:08:28.073
It's already hurt Doug.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.943
I don't want any more of the
judges to hurt themselves.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.011
We'll see what happens.

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:03.742
 Sam, in the world of
weapons and warriors,

00:09:03.809 --> 00:09:06.178
a weapon should be
feared by your enemy,

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:08.414
not by the warrior
who wields it.

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:10.449
Because that pommel
is so out of scale

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:14.219
and inflicted so much harm to
Doug in that first kill test,

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:17.856
that in the strength test
we just can't take the risk

00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:19.925
of injuring one of our judges.

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:23.629
And for that reason, I'd like to
invite you to shake our hands,

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:26.832
shake your competitors hand,
and then please leave the forge.

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:32.738
It looks fantastic, man.

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:35.407
 I'm not surprised
at the judge's ruling.

00:09:35.474 --> 00:09:36.875
I totally agree
with what they said.

00:09:36.975 --> 00:09:39.645
I may not be the Forged
in Fire Champion,

00:09:39.712 --> 00:09:41.647
but I got to use
the power hammer.

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:44.550
And I got to make an
excellent blade and cool mace.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.985
So I'm really happy.

00:09:49.822 --> 00:09:53.225
 Jason, your weapon has
elevated you to the title

00:09:53.325 --> 00:09:54.827
of Forged in Fire Champion.

00:09:54.893 --> 00:09:57.195
And you'll be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:09:57.295 --> 00:09:57.964
Good job, brother.

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:05.003
 I'm absolutely astounded.

00:10:05.103 --> 00:10:06.138
I won.

00:10:06.205 --> 00:10:09.208
I feel very, very lucky
and so very thankful.

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:10.542
Being the Forged
in Fire Champion

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:12.711
means that it
validates my skills.

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.713
And I'm able to
look at my children

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.515
and I can say,
follow your dreams.

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:17.649
Chase them.

00:10:17.716 --> 00:10:19.986
You can achieve anything.

